Turn creature_template damage-school immunity into an 80% resist.
Touches: src/server/game/Entities/Unit/Unit.h, src/server/game/Entities/Unit/Unit.cpp

Why: player report -- "enemy resistances should cap at 80% so that mobs
immune to certain damage types don't exist (but still resist a significant
amount of damage that they were previously immune to)". Patch 0002 already
caps the discrete RESIST roll at 80%, but that only governs the resistance
formula. It has nothing to say about outright immunity, which is a separate
mechanism: Unit::IsImmunedToDamage / IsImmunedToSchool short-circuit the
damage long before CalcAbsorbResist ever runs, so a Fire-immune mob was
still taking exactly zero from every Fire spell no matter what patch 0002
did.

Scope: creature_template immunities ONLY. Creature::LoadTemplateImmunities
registers template-sourced entries under a sentinel spell id (uint32 max)
specifically so they can be told apart from aura-sourced ones -- the core
already relies on that distinction itself in
IgnoresSchoolImmunityFromFriendlyCaster. Using the same test means a boss
that goes invulnerable for a phase (a real spell, real aura) is completely
unaffected, and so is every player immunity (Divine Shield, Ice Block,
Anti-Magic Shell) since the check bails on !IsCreature() first. If a
template-immune creature additionally gains a real immunity aura covering
the same school, the aura wins and it is genuinely immune again.

Known limit: CalcAbsorbResist's resist block does not run for physical
(SPELL_SCHOOL_MASK_NORMAL) damage, so a creature with template PHYSICAL
immunity stops being immune but does not pick up the 80% resist -- it would
take full melee damage. No such creature is known to be reachable in open
world content here; revisit if one turns up.

Gated by LivingGear.SoftenCreatureImmunity (default 1), read via
LivingGear_SoftenCreatureImmunity() in LivingGear_Perks.cpp.

--- a/src/server/game/Entities/Unit/Unit.h
+++ b/src/server/game/Entities/Unit/Unit.h
@@ near GetSchoolImmunityMask/GetDamageImmunityMask
     [[nodiscard]] uint32 GetSchoolImmunityMask() const;
     [[nodiscard]] uint32 GetDamageImmunityMask() const;
+
+    // Living Gear core-patch: true "this school cannot hurt me at all"
+    // invulnerability coming from creature_template is downgraded to an 80%
+    // resist. Template-sourced immunity only -- see the implementation.
+    [[nodiscard]] bool LivingGearSoftenedSchoolImmunity(SpellSchoolMask schoolMask) const;

--- a/src/server/game/Entities/Unit/Unit.cpp
+++ b/src/server/game/Entities/Unit/Unit.cpp
@@ above Unit::GetDamageImmunityMask()
+bool LivingGear_SoftenCreatureImmunity();
+
+bool Unit::LivingGearSoftenedSchoolImmunity(SpellSchoolMask schoolMask) const
+{
+    static uint32 constexpr templateSpellId = std::numeric_limits<uint32>::max();
+
+    if (schoolMask == SPELL_SCHOOL_MASK_NONE || !IsCreature())
+        return false;
+    if (!LivingGear_SoftenCreatureImmunity())
+        return false;
+
+    uint32 templateMask = 0;
+    uint32 auraMask = 0;
+    for (uint32 op : { uint32(IMMUNITY_SCHOOL), uint32(IMMUNITY_DAMAGE) })
+        for (auto const& [immunitySchoolMask, immunityAuraId] : m_spellImmune[op])
+        {
+            if (immunityAuraId == templateSpellId)
+                templateMask |= immunitySchoolMask;
+            else
+                auraMask |= immunitySchoolMask;
+        }
+
+    return Unit::IsImmuneMaskFully(SpellSchoolMask(templateMask), schoolMask)
+        && !Unit::IsImmuneMaskFully(SpellSchoolMask(auraMask), schoolMask);
+}

@@ Unit::IsImmunedToDamage(SpellSchoolMask), Unit::IsImmunedToDamage(Unit const*, SpellInfo const*), Unit::IsImmunedToSchool(SpellSchoolMask)
     if (schoolMask == SPELL_SCHOOL_MASK_NONE)
         return false;

+    if (LivingGearSoftenedSchoolImmunity(schoolMask))
+        return false;
+

@@ Unit::CalcAbsorbResist(), immediately after patch 0002's cap
         if (i > 8)
             i = 8;

+        // A creature whose template says it is flat-out immune to this school
+        // resists 80% instead. Without this it would take FULL damage, since
+        // the immunity checks above now deliberately report "not immune" in
+        // order to get the hit this far.
+        if (victim->LivingGearSoftenedSchoolImmunity(schoolMask))
+            i = 8;
